      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Do not use superglue on an open wound, as it causes severe tissue damage and creates a breeding ground for bacteria instead of protecting the injury. Hydrogen peroxide is also inappropriate for cleaning wounds because it damages healthy tissue cells and delays the body's natural healing process. Stick to washing with soap and water only, then apply an antibiotic ointment under a sterile bandage to seal the area effectively. Since rust can introduce significant toxins like iron ore, please reconsider finishing your work in the garden until you consult a doctor.",
